          "prompt": "Find the centroid $\\sigma_a$ of the asymptotes of $G(s) = \\frac{K}{s(s+{{a}})(s+{{b}})}$.",
          "answer": "-(a+b)/3",
          "unit": "",
          "explanation": "Poles: 0, $-{{a}}$, $-{{b}}$; no zeros, so $n - m = 3$. $\\sigma_a = \\frac{0 - {{a}} - {{b}}}{3}$ = {{-(a+b)/3}}. The three asymptotes leave from there at ±60° and 180°."
